config FREETZ_PACKAGE_DOMOTICZ_IDETECT
	bool "Domoticz plugin: presence detection from the router (iDetect)"
	depends on FREETZ_PACKAGE_DOMOTICZ
	select FREETZ_PACKAGE_PYTHON3_FRITZCONNECTION
	select FREETZ_PACKAGE_PYTHON3_PARAMIKO
	select FREETZ_PACKAGE_PYTHON3_PYNETGEAR
	select FREETZ_PACKAGE_PYTHON3_REQUESTS
	default n
	help
		presence detection driven by the clients of the home router: the
		devices that the router lists as connected are reported as
		present in Domoticz

		It is a Python plugin of Domoticz: the package installs it into
		/usr/share/domoticz/plugins/Domoticz_iDetect, the directory Domoticz is
		started with (-approot of the domoticz package), and it needs no
		change of the Domoticz build.

		The plugin needs python3-fritzconnection, python-paramiko,
		pynetgear and requests (installed as dependencies of this
		package) in addition to the standard library: the trackers of the
		repository query the router over TR-064, SSH, HTTP or the SOAP
		API of NETGEAR. The supported routers include FRITZ!Box, OpenWrt
		(brctl), RouterOS, UniFi, USG, Zyxel, NETGEAR, TP-Link Omada,
		Orbi, AiMesh and every host that answers a ping; the credentials
		and the tracker to use are the settings of the plugin.

		Setup: Setup -> Hardware -> iDetect, choose the tracker of the
		router and enter its address and credentials.

		The upstream repository has no release tags, so the build fetches a
		pinned commit of the default branch. Upstream ships no license
		file: the README and the images it refers to are installed with
		the plugin.
